Pradeep Kumar Jha, IIT Roorkee. Principles of Metal Forming Technology, NPTEL 112107250. [Official course](https://nptel.ac.in/courses/112107250) · [Complete eight-week syllabus](https://archive.nptel.ac.in/content/syllabus_pdf/112107250.pdf).

Complete the whole public sequence and its derivations/examples: stress/strain, flow/yield relations, instability, temperature/rate effects, mechanics/analysis, forging, rolling, extrusion, drawing, sheet operations, defects, and powder forming. Compare idealized calculations with metallurgical state, friction, heat, geometry, and observed products.

Instructor, full syllabus, scope, and public course route were verified on 29 October 2026. Course-run/exam registration is separate from learning; public access does not establish unrestricted redistribution or access to every campus assessment. Preserve actual media/component rights and revision information. All source media remain external.

